      },
      "pinnedBy": null,
      "body": "I ... am getting annoyed by the dynamic parameter APIs. \n\nHere's what we do. Check if the parameter name starts with `plugin_name_`. If it doesn't, then `continue` in the loop. That way we skip any non-this-plugin parameters set. \n\nHeck, that might also be the solution for MPPI with the non-MPPI parameter changes triggering resets we've been talking about over Slack. Lets do that in MPPI too. \n\nThen, we can rearrange this ticket to updating all Plugins to do the same, since all plugin's parameters are or should be under the plugin's root namespace. I think this is a good global change. ",
      "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I ... am getting annoyed by the dynamic parameter APIs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here's what we do. Check if the parameter name starts with <code class=\"notranslate\">plugin_name_</code>. If it doesn't, then <code class=\"notranslate\">continue</code> in the loop. That way we skip any non-this-plugin parameters set.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Heck, that might also be the solution for MPPI with the non-MPPI parameter changes triggering resets we've been talking about over Slack. Lets do that in MPPI too.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Then, we can rearrange this ticket to updating all Plugins to do the same, since all plugin's parameters are or should be under the plugin's root namespace. I think this is a good global change.</p>",
      "bodyVersion": "4c27b5d0d60241c6f029d9e94f4aec5362ba33737d71761c823cdf1148c8ee88",
